---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";
import Stamp from "../../components/Stamp.astro";
import headerBand from "../../ornaments/header-band.svg?raw";

const plates = [
  {
    numeral: "Plate I",
    title: "One platform, three agencies",
    lede: "The same platform, sold to a second and third client instead of rebuilt.",
    body: [
      "A national land agency needed its teams to make data-informed decisions on land availability, legal status and utilisation. We built the platform once. When a mining company and then a sovereign fund needed something adjacent, the answer was configuration, not a new codebase: the same spatial identity, the same catalogue, the same delivery surface, with their data and their analysis on top.",
      "The first client is now on its third phase. That is the number I care about most, because a renewal is harder to fake than a new logo.",
    ],
    facts: [
      { value: "3", label: "clients on one platform" },
      { value: "3", label: "phases with the first" },
      { value: "1 mo", label: "to first delivery" },
      { value: "2", label: "engineers, one data lead" },
    ],
  },
  {
    numeral: "Plate II",
    title: "Population where it actually lives",
    lede: "A dasymetric framework that puts age cohorts on a 50 m grid using open data only.",
    body: [
      "Village totals are the wrong unit for exposure. RIUH redistributes population onto a 50 m grid across five generational cohorts, using distance-decay accessibility surfaces, open POIs and modelled building density, and preserves the official village totals exactly.",
      "The method is multi-algorithmic, and building density dominates feature importance. Ridge regression reaches an R² of 0.94 for Gen Z and 0.92 for Gen Alpha. Everything is reproducible and built from open data, which matters in places where the commercial alternative is a licence nobody can afford.",
      "The same surface is now being pushed toward meso-scale traffic simulation, because buying traffic data in Indonesia is both expensive and unscalable.",
    ],
    facts: [
      { value: "50 m", label: "cell size" },
      { value: "5", label: "age cohorts" },
      { value: "0.94", label: "R², Gen Z" },
      { value: "100%", label: "open data" },
    ],
  },
  {
    numeral: "Plate III",
    title: "The bill and the bus factor",
    lede: "Precompute once, serve cheaply, and make sure more than two people can run it.",
    body: [
      "On-demand compute is the right tool for exploration and the wrong tool for serving a layer that never changes. Moving the serving path to batch precomputation, with Cloud Optimised GeoTIFF, GeoParquet and PMTiles behind a thin tile server, cut total infrastructure cost by 32% and made analysis roughly four times faster.",
      "The cost curve is the argument. Serving every national dataset now costs about $23 a month, and the eleventh client on the same data costs about $20 more than the first. One client pays for the map; the rest are nearly free.",
      "I also care that the pipeline survives me. When I started, two people could run it end to end. It is five now, and that is the change I would defend hardest.",
    ],
    facts: [
      { value: "-32%", label: "total infrastructure" },
      { value: "$23", label: "per national dataset" },
      { value: "4x", label: "faster analysis" },
      { value: "2 to 5", label: "people who can run it" },
    ],
    note: "Infrastructure is reviewed in aggregate. Per-deal margin is not tracked, and I would rather say so than invent a number.",
  },
];

const pipeline = [
  { step: "01", title: "Sources", note: "open, licensed, partner and uploaded data" },
  { step: "02", title: "Batch precompute", note: "validate, harmonise, calculate once" },
  { step: "03", title: "Static store", note: "COG, GeoParquet, PMTiles" },
  { step: "04", title: "Thin server", note: "tiles and reads, no recomputation" },
  { step: "05", title: "Client", note: "map, report, export or API" },
];
---
<Base
  title="Work — Azzadiva Sawungrana"
  description="Three pieces of work: a platform resold to three agencies, a dasymetric population framework, and the migration that cut infrastructure cost by a third."
>
  <div class="ornament w-full text-ink/30" aria-hidden="true" set:html={headerBand}></div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6">
    <header class="mt-8 md:mt-12">
      <p class="stamp-text text-ink-soft">selected work</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[2rem] leading-[1.12] text-ink-deep md:text-[2.5rem]">
        Three things worth explaining properly.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[1.08rem]">
        Not a portfolio. Three projects where the decision was interesting, the number is checkable,
        and the thing I would do differently is easy to name.
      </p>
    </header>

    <Rule />

    <div class="space-y-16 pb-4">
      {
        plates.map((plate) => (
          <section class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-[7rem_1fr] md:gap-8">
            <div class="pt-1">
              <Stamp label={plate.numeral} />
            </div>
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-[1.45rem] leading-snug text-ink-deep md:text-[1.6rem]">
                {plate.title}
              </h2>
              <p class="mt-2 text-[1.05rem] text-ink">{plate.lede}</p>

              <div class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-3">
                {plate.body.map((p) => (
                  <p class="text-[0.98rem]">{p}</p>
                ))}
              </div>

              <dl class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-4 border-y rule-line py-4 sm:grid-cols-4">
                {plate.facts.map((f) => (
                  <div class="flex flex-col-reverse">
                    <dt class="stamp-text mt-1.5 text-ink-soft">{f.label}</dt>
                    <dd class="text-[1.35rem] leading-none text-ink-deep">{f.value}</dd>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </dl>

              {plate.note && (
                <p class="mt-3 text-[0.88rem] italic text-ink-soft">{plate.note}</p>
              )}

              {plate.numeral === "Plate III" && (
                <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-5" aria-label="serving pipeline">
                  {pipeline.map((s) => (
                    <li class="plate-frame bg-paper-deep/40 px-3 py-3">
                      <p class="stamp-text text-accent">{s.step}</p>
                      <p class="mt-1 text-[0.92rem] leading-tight text-ink-deep">{s.title}</p>
                      <p class="mt-1 text-[0.8rem] leading-snug text-ink-soft">{s.note}</p>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ol>
              )}
            </div>
          </section>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <Rule />

    <p class="max-w-2xl pb-10 text-[0.92rem] text-ink-soft">
      Client names are left out where agreements ask for it, and contract values are not published.
      Happy to go into detail in a conversation.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
